  "root_node": "source.raw.lineitem",
  "cause": "upstream_data",
  "action": "escalate",
  "evidence": "The failing dbt checks not_null_stg_lineitem_order_key and not_null_stg_lineitem_order_line_id each reported 1550 failing rows. In stg_lineitem, order_key is directly taken from raw.lineitem.l_orderkey, and order_line_id is built from l_orderkey and l_linenumber. A query on raw.lineitem shows 1550 rows where l_orderkey is NULL (null_orderkey = 1550) while l_linenumber has no nulls. Therefore the null order_key values originate in the source raw.lineitem table, causing the downstream not‑null checks to fail. The issue is upstream data, so it should be escalated to the source owner."
}
